4 Faculty/Division: VP-Facilities & Real Estate Department: Food Services Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Banquet Server is responsible for food and drink serving duties while interacting with guests in positive, friendly, and efficient manner. Pillars for this position include tact, diplomacy, attention to detail, accuracy, and integrity. Typical Duties: Review Banquet Event Order (BEO`s) at the beginning of each shift to ensure rooms are set as contracted. Set up for events by putting out place settings, arranging table placement and setting up a buffet. Maintaining proper dining experience, delivering items, fulfilling customer needs, removing courses, replenishing utensils, refilling glasses. Understands and can communicate products and services available at the Convention Centre Perform cleaning tasks and breakdown of service. Communicate any areas of need, problems, and concerns from guests to Banquet Supervisor. Greet all guests warmly with an appropriate greeting. Adhere to grooming and appearance standards consistently. Provide all group guests with a lasting experience of the Convention Centre with intent for return business. Ensure proper use, storage of all banquet equipment. Maintain high standards of safety and cleanliness in all areas of the Convention Centre. Qualifications Education: High School diploma or GED Experience: Previous serving experience. Other: Excellent oral communication skills. Positive interpersonal skills. Must speak English and be able to write in English. Smart Serve certification. Please note: This is for four (4) vacancies Closing Date: 09/11/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: C3261Cas 89ChNt Appointment Type : Ancillary Operations Schedule: Part-Time, Casual, Flexible schedule required, which may include evening and weekend hours Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: $20.00 per hour Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of To